   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "a road change regenerates the tiles it touches, not the global graph.",
   "originalText": "a road change regenerates the tiles it touches, not the global graph.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 550,
   "width": 777,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100024,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700168,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The search loads a tile, traverses it, and on reaching a boundary node FETCHES THE NEIGHBOUR AND\nSTITCHES IT IN, continuing seamlessly. So the working set is the corridor the route actually\ntraverses, not the whole world.",
   "originalText": "The search loads a tile, traverses it, and on reaching a boundary node FETCHES THE NEIGHBOUR AND\nSTITCHES IT IN, continuing seamlessly. So the working set is the corridor the route actually\ntraverses, not the whole world.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 620,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100025,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700175,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The cost is boundary bookkeeping: a node on a tile edge appears in both tiles, and the search must\nnot double-count it or lose a road that crosses the boundary. A real source of subtle bugs - a\nmissing boundary reference manifests as 'the router refuses to use this road', which is very hard to\nnotice and very annoying when it happens.",
   "originalText": "The cost is boundary bookkeeping: a node on a tile edge appears in both tiles, and the search must\nnot double-count it or lose a road that crosses the boundary. A real source of subtle bugs - a\nmissing boundary reference manifests as 'the router refuses to use this road', which is very hard to\nnotice and very annoying when it happens.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
