  },
  {
   "id": "ld3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1180,
   "y": 880,
   "width": 442,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100043,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700301,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "MOTORWAYS ONLY - a few thousand edges for a whole continent",
   "originalText": "MOTORWAYS ONLY - a few thousand edges for a whole continent",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ph",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 926,
   "width": 820,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100044,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700308,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "ph_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ph_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 941,
   "width": 804,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100045,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700315,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. ESCAPE   search level 0 near the origin until you reach a motorway on-ramp\n2. CRUISE   search LEVEL 3 across the country - thousands of edges, not tens\n            of millions\n3. ARRIVE   drop back to level 0 near the destination",
   "originalText": "1. ESCAPE   search level 0 near the origin until you reach a motorway on-ramp\n2. CRUISE   search LEVEL 3 across the country - thousands of edges, not tens\n            of millions\n3. ARRIVE   drop back to level 0 near the destination",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "ph",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 926,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100046,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700322,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The middle phase is where the win is: crossing a continent on a motorway-only\ngraph is THREE TO FOUR ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE less work. And it matches the correct\nanswer - a 600 km route DOES use motorways in the middle, so searching\nresidential streets in between was not merely expensive, it was searching a space\nthe answer is not in.",
   "originalText": "The middle phase is where the win is: crossing a continent on a motorway-only\ngraph is THREE TO FOUR ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE less work. And it matches the correct\nanswer - a 600 km route DOES use motorways in the middle, so searching\nresidential streets in between was not merely expensive, it was searching a space\nthe answer is not in.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1022,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100047,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700329,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Same idea as a sparse index: do not search at full resolution when a coarse pass\nplus local refinement gets the same answer far cheaper.",
   "originalText": "Same idea as a sparse index: do not search at full resolution when a coarse pass\nplus local refinement gets the same answer far cheaper.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1046,
   "width": 810,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100048,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700336,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The honest limitation: hierarchical routing is an APPROXIMATION. It can miss a route that would have\nbeen slightly faster via a clever sequence of arterial roads, because the coarse pass never\nconsidered them. Production systems mitigate this by overlapping levels (level 3 includes some major\narterials, not strictly motorways) and by widening the search near level junctions - and they accept\na route that is 'very good' rather than provably optimal. Given the accuracy requirement is about\nCORRECT INSTRUCTIONS rather than provably minimal time, that is the right trade - but it should be\nstated, not glossed.",
   "originalText": "The honest limitation: hierarchical routing is an APPROXIMATION. It can miss a route that would have\nbeen slightly faster via a clever sequence of arterial roads, because the coarse pass never\nconsidered them. Production systems mitigate this by overlapping levels (level 3 includes some major\narterials, not strictly motorways) and by widening the search near level junctions - and they accept\na route that is 'very good' rather than provably optimal. Given the accuracy requirement is about\nCORRECT INSTRUCTIONS rather than provably minimal time, that is the right trade - but it should be\nstated, not glossed.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
