   "containerId": "gr",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "wt",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1540,
   "width": 780,
   "height": 50,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "#fecaca",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "wt_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "wt_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1557,
   "width": 764,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100060,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700420,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the WEIGHTS   how long each takes right now      ->   changes CONSTANTLY, seconds",
   "originalText": "the WEIGHTS   how long each takes right now      ->   changes CONSTANTLY, seconds",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "wt",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 1476,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100061,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700427,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Baking weights into the tiles would mean REPUBLISHING ROUTING TILES EVERY TIME\nTRAFFIC CHANGED - the equivalent of publishing a new map version every few\nseconds. So tiles carry only static properties (geometry, speed limit, road\nclass, turn restrictions) and live weights are looked up separately by segment\nid.",
   "originalText": "Baking weights into the tiles would mean REPUBLISHING ROUTING TILES EVERY TIME\nTRAFFIC CHANGED - the equivalent of publishing a new map version every few\nseconds. So tiles carry only static properties (geometry, speed limit, road\nclass, turn restrictions) and live weights are looked up separately by segment\nid.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 1568,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100062,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700434,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "That separation buys three things: the ETA model retrains and redeploys on its own\ncadence; the routing tiles stay immutable and cacheable; and if ETA is\nunavailable, falling back to static speed limits leaves routes CORRECT BUT\nAPPROXIMATELY TIMED - losing the enhancement while keeping the function.",
   "originalText": "That separation buys three things: the ETA model retrains and redeploys on its own\ncadence; the routing tiles stay immutable and cacheable; and if ETA is\nunavailable, falling back to static speed limits leaves routes CORRECT BUT\nAPPROXIMATELY TIMED - losing the enhancement while keeping the function.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1620,
   "width": 801,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100063,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700441,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The model predicts per-segment travel time from live speeds (aggregated from GPS samples),\nhistorical patterns by time-of-day and day-of-week, road class, weather and known events. The\nhistorical part is what makes a route requested for 8am TOMORROW meaningful, since there is no live\ntraffic for the future - which is the reason the model cannot just be a live-speed lookup.",
   "originalText": "The model predicts per-segment travel time from live speeds (aggregated from GPS samples),\nhistorical patterns by time-of-day and day-of-week, road class, weather and known events. The\nhistorical part is what makes a route requested for 8am TOMORROW meaningful, since there is no live\ntraffic for the future - which is the reason the model cannot just be a live-speed lookup.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d6",
