  {
   "id": "fl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1718,
   "width": 794,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100065,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700455,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "An incident occurs. Which of millions of in-flight navigators are affected?",
   "originalText": "An incident occurs. Which of millions of in-flight navigators are affected?",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "naive",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1756,
   "width": 820,
   "height": 74,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100066,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700462,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "naive_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "naive_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1770,
   "width": 804,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100067,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700469,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the naive answer - store each user's full route as a list of tiles\n  user_1: r_1, r_2, r_3, ..., r_k        # a 600 km route = HUNDREDS of tiles\n  user_2: r_4, r_6, r_9, ..., r_n",
   "originalText": "the naive answer - store each user's full route as a list of tiles\n  user_1: r_1, r_2, r_3, ..., r_k        # a 600 km route = HUNDREDS of tiles\n  user_2: r_4, r_6, r_9, ..., r_n",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "naive",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1756,
   "width": 539,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100068,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700476,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "At millions of concurrent navigators x hundreds of tiles each, that is a\nbillion-row structure to scan on EVERY incident.",
   "originalText": "At millions of concurrent navigators x hundreds of tiles each, that is a\nbillion-row structure to scan on EVERY incident.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "multi",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1856,
   "width": 820,
   "height": 54,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100069,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700483,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "multi_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "multi_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1868,
   "width": 804,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100070,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700490,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "store the route at MULTIPLE RESOLUTIONS instead\n  user_1: r_1, super(r_1), super(super(r_1)), ...   # a handful of entries",
   "originalText": "store the route at MULTIPLE RESOLUTIONS instead\n  user_1: r_1, super(r_1), super(super(r_1)), ...   # a handful of entries",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "multi",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1856,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100071,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700497,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Because coarse tiles CONTAIN fine tiles, a whole route summarizes as a small set\nof progressively coarser tiles. So the check becomes: does the incident's tile\nfall within any of the user's coarse tiles? A containment test against a handful\nof entries rather than a scan of hundreds.",
   "originalText": "Because coarse tiles CONTAIN fine tiles, a whole route summarizes as a small set\nof progressively coarser tiles. So the check becomes: does the incident's tile\nfall within any of the user's coarse tiles? A containment test against a handful\nof entries rather than a scan of hundreds.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1940,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100072,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The trade is precision: a coarse tile covering a large region matches users whose route passes NEAR the incident but not\nthrough it - false positives. So the flow is two-stage: COARSE CONTAINMENT TO SHORTLIST, THEN RECOMPUTE THOSE ROUTES TO KNOW\nFOR CERTAIN. A filter-then-verify pattern, and the same shape as the geospatial boundary problem: the index narrows, an exact\ncheck decides.",
   "originalText": "The trade is precision: a coarse tile covering a large region matches users whose route passes NEAR the incident but not\nthrough it - false positives. So the flow is two-stage: COARSE CONTAINMENT TO SHORTLIST, THEN RECOMPUTE THOSE ROUTES TO KNOW\nFOR CERTAIN. A filter-then-verify pattern, and the same shape as the geospatial boundary problem: the index narrows, an exact\ncheck decides.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fn4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2020,
   "width": 995,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100073,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700511,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And a reroute is only OFFERED if it is materially better. Interrupting a driver to save 40 seconds is a worse product than\nsaying nothing, so the threshold is a product decision - typically minutes, not seconds - sitting on top of the technical\nmechanism. Delivery is over WebSocket: mobile push has payload limits and does not exist on web, and polling would wake the\nradio repeatedly on a device where battery is a first-class requirement.",
   "originalText": "And a reroute is only OFFERED if it is materially better. Interrupting a driver to save 40 seconds is a worse product than\nsaying nothing, so the threshold is a product decision - typically minutes, not seconds - sitting on top of the technical\nmechanism. Delivery is over WebSocket: mobile push has payload limits and does not exist on web, and polling would wake the\nradio repeatedly on a device where battery is a first-class requirement.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d7",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2110,
   "width": 1680,
